flowchart TB
    accTitle: Development feedback ends before final outcomes
    accDescr: The eight development tasks support a loop of pilot runs, inspection, and revisions. Before final evaluation, freeze the tested code, policies, model configuration, budgets, fixtures, graders, and metrics in a manifest. The sixteen final tasks are validated with model-free controls and identified in the manifest. A launcher validates that manifest before final agent trials. Final outcomes feed the report, not changes to the frozen study.
    P["Pilot on 8 development tasks"]
    P -->|"Revise and rerun"| P
    P -->|"Activation + boundary tests pass"| F["Freeze experiment manifest"]
    T["16 final tasks: model-free controls"] --> F
    F --> V("Manifest valid?")
    V -->|"No"| B["Block launch"]
    V -->|"Yes"| E["Run final agent trials"]
    E --> O["Audit outcomes and report"]
